# 5. USER ROLES AND PERMISSIONS

Kea Parrot MUST use centralized, server-enforced authorization.

## 5.1 User Roles

### Guest
- Browse public content.
- View public polls and results.
- View public game descriptions.
- Open shared public activity links.
- Vote in polls and play the 3 games within the guest participation window (Guest Session Rule, §6.4).
- Cannot publish content.
- Cannot comment.
- Cannot react.
- Cannot join communities.
- Cannot report content.
- Cannot create game records associated with an account.
- Cannot access private profiles.

### Registered User
- Create posts.
- Publish anonymously or with attribution.
- Comment.
- React.
- Vote.
- Play games.
- View personal activity.
- Report content.
- Block users.
- Manage privacy settings.

### Moderator
- Review reports.
- Hide or remove violating content.
- Apply authorized restrictions.
- Review moderation history.
- Escalate serious incidents.

### Administrator
- Manage platform configuration.
- Manage users and moderators.
- Review audit logs.
- Manage content and enforcement.
- Access authorized operational dashboards.

### Super Administrator
- Manage privileged administrative operations.
- Assign administrator and moderator roles.
- Manage critical system configuration.
- Review security events.

Privileged administrative access MUST be protected by stronger authentication and must never be assignable through ordinary user-facing APIs.

Role storage (D-18, decided 2026-11-20): roles are stored in the `user_roles` table (KEA-DBS-002 §4.9) and resolved server-side only; `profiles` has no role column and a role is never taken from client claims.

## 5.2 Permission Principles

- Users can modify only their own permitted resources.
- Anonymous publishing must not remove internal account accountability.
- Moderators cannot assign themselves administrator privileges.
- Administrators cannot bypass immutable audit records.
- All privileged actions must be logged.
- Authorization must be validated server-side.

