# 6. AUTHENTICATION AND ACCOUNT MANAGEMENT

## 6.1 Registration

Requirement: AUTH-001.

Users must be able to register using the supported authentication methods:

- Email and password.
- Supported OAuth providers, when explicitly configured.

MVP authentication will use Supabase Auth.

Requirements:

1. Validate email addresses.
2. Enforce password policy.
3. Provide email verification.
4. Prevent duplicate account creation.
5. Provide secure login and logout.
6. Provide password reset.
7. Provide session management.
8. Handle expired sessions.
9. Provide appropriate authentication error messages.
10. Never expose authentication secrets to the browser.

OAuth providers must not be displayed as available unless configured and tested.

## 6.2 Age Eligibility

Requirement: AUTH-002.

The initial public MVP is restricted to users aged 16+.

Users aged 16–17 are included in the 16+ audience; there is no adult-only content in the MVP; Ghana Data Protection Act 2012 (Act 843) / DPC review is still required before public launch. Parental-consent mechanism: legal-review item (TBD, owner Dennis, before public launch) — do not invent.

Requirements:

- Display the age eligibility notice.
- Collect the minimum necessary age confirmation.
- Prevent underage users from completing registration.
- Record the relevant consent and policy version.
- Do not expose date of birth publicly.
- Do not assume that self-declaration constitutes legally sufficient age verification in every market.

Expansion to younger users requires separate legal and safety approval.

## 6.3 User Profiles

Requirement: AUTH-003.

Each registered user must have:

- Unique internal user ID.
- Unique username.
- Display name.
- Optional avatar.
- Optional biography.
- Account creation timestamp.
- Profile visibility setting.
- Account status.
- Achievement summary when available.

Profile information must be validated and sanitized.

Public profiles must not expose:

- Email address.
- Authentication identifiers.
- Internal moderation records.
- Private account metadata.
- Exact location history.

## 6.4 Guest Browsing

Requirement: AUTH-004.

Unauthenticated visitors may browse public discovery content.

When they attempt an authenticated action, display a clear registration or login prompt.

Guest browsing must not expose restricted content or private user information.

**Guest Session Rule (D-03, canonical — owner decision 2026-11-20).** A guest is an unauthenticated visitor, identified by a server-issued guest-session token stored in the browser. A guest is NOT an account. A guest MAY: browse public discovery; view polls/results and game descriptions; vote in polls; play the 3 games. A guest may NOT: post, comment, react, join communities, report content, or create any game record associated with an account. (Guest game sessions are tied to the guest session only, never to an account.) LIMITED TIME: a guest participation window lasts **60 minutes from the guest session's first vote or game start**, and ends on browser close, whichever is first. After expiry the guest must register / log in to vote or play again. One vote per poll per guest session. Guest votes are counted. Guest game scores are not saved to a profile and do not appear on leaderboards. After registration, guest-session votes/scores do NOT transfer to the new account (no merge in MVP). Rate limits apply per guest session + IP (thresholds TBD in Product P1 config — do not invent). Guests may NOT change/remove a vote.

