# 9. SOCIAL CONTENT MODULE

Module ID: SOCIAL

## 9.1 Supported Content Types

MVP content types:

1. Text notes.
2. Questions.
3. Poll-linked posts.

Image and audio uploads are not included in the initial MVP.

## 9.2 Post Creation

Requirement: SOCIAL-001.

Authenticated users can create posts.

Required fields:

- Content body.
- Content type.
- Publishing identity mode.
- Optional community association.
- Optional approximate area association.

Publishing identity modes:

- Attributed.
- Anonymous.

Anonymous posts must still reference the authenticated account internally.

## 9.3 Content Validation

Requirement: SOCIAL-002.

The system must:

- Validate text length.
- Reject empty posts.
- Normalize input safely.
- Prevent executable HTML and script injection.
- Apply spam controls.
- Apply rate limits.
- Apply content moderation.
- Reject prohibited content under the platform policy.

Exact maximum character limits must be defined in centrally maintained product configuration before implementation.

Do not independently invent different limits in different screens or endpoints.

## 9.4 Reactions

Requirement: SOCIAL-003.

Users may react to eligible posts.

MVP reaction set:

- Like.
- Funny.
- Interesting.
- Surprising.

Rules:

- One active reaction per user per post.
- Users can change their reaction.
- Users can remove their reaction.
- Reaction counts must remain accurate.
- Reactions must not bypass blocked-user restrictions.

## 9.5 Comments

Requirement: SOCIAL-004.

Authenticated users may comment on eligible posts.

MVP rules:

- Text comments only.
- Comment ownership.
- Comment editing within a centrally configured period.
- Comment deletion by its author.
- Moderation removal.
- Reporting.
- Pagination.

Comments must respect the visibility and moderation state of their parent content.

## 9.6 Content Expiration

Requirement: SOCIAL-005.

MVP posts are persistent unless removed by their owner or moderation action.

Temporary location-based content is reserved for Product P3.

