# 13. LOCATION AND GEOSPATIAL MODULE

Module ID: LOC

## 13.1 MVP Location Requirements

The initial MVP supports:

- Manually selected areas.
- Approximate browser-provided location.
- Area-based discovery.
- Public content associated with approximate geographic areas.

## 13.2 Privacy Rules

- Exact user coordinates must never appear in public API responses.
- Exact coordinates must not be displayed to other users.
- Do not maintain unnecessary historical location records.
- Do not perform background location tracking.
- Do not request location permission without a clear user action.
- Do not expose the identity of users currently occupying a location.
- Apply minimum aggregation thresholds to sensitive location-based statistics.

## 13.3 Geospatial Technology

Use PostgreSQL with PostGIS.

Use spatial indexes for nearby content queries.

The implementation must document:

- Coordinate reference system.
- Approximation strategy.
- Search radius.
- Geographic boundaries.
- Index strategy.
- Query performance.

The precise initial search radius must be a centrally configured product setting approved before implementation.

